{"_v":1,"id":"shrek-the-musical-2008","cat":"broadway","cs":72.1,"rc":5,"bd":{"positive":3,"mixed":2,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Chris Jones","o":"Chicago Tribune","s":66,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.newspapers.com/image/232075947/","d":"2008-12-15","q":"Given the givens, there's a lot to admire and enjoy."},{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":63,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2008/12/15/theater/reviews/15shrek.html","d":"2008-12-15","q":"Aside from a few jolly sequences (nearly all featuring the hypertalented Ms. Foster), this cavalcade of storybook effigies feels like 40 blocks’ worth of a Macy’s Thanksgiving Day Parade, accompanied by an exhaustingly jokey running commentary."},{"cn":"Eric March","o":"Theater Life","s":81,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://theaterlife.com/shrek-the-musical/","d":"2009-08-13","q":"And adults, too, will enjoy this gleeful staging."},{"cn":"Joe Dziemianowicz","o":"New York Daily News","s":75,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.newspapers.com/image/393092795/","d":"2008-12-15","q":"Shrek the Musical joins the ranks of things that work, even if it's ungainly."},{"cn":"Lucy Komisar","o":"The Komisar Scoop","s":88,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://www.thekomisarscoop.com/2009/12/shrek-the-musical-is-a-kids-show-with-clever-jokes-lyrics-for-adults/","d":"2009-12-04","q":"The characters in the first play fight oppression, the second combat racism and Shrek does a bit of both. Like the others, it proves that shows about ideas are more interesting and fun than empty-headed fluff. Book and lyrics are by David Lindsay-Abaire, who has a long track record of writing clever satires for adults."}],"au":{"score":76,"designation":"Shrugging","sources":{"mz":{"s":76,"c":227,"sr":3.8}}},"tn":[{"yr":63,"cat":"Best Costume Design of a Musical","n":"Tim Hatley","w":true},{"yr":63,"cat":"Best Musical","n":null},{"yr":63,"cat":"Best Book of a Musical","n":"David Lindsay-Abaire"},{"yr":63,"cat":"Best Original Score","n":"Jea